          players: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: Optional',
          deck: 'Type: 32-card deck (strip 2-6 from standard pack). Cards 7-10, J, Q, K, A in four suits. One deck.\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included',
          equipment: '32-card deck (or strip 2-6 from standard deck)\nChips or tokens (e.g. 3 per player)\nTable space',
          dealing: 'Dealer gives 3 cards face down to each player plus one extra hand of 3 cards. Dealer chooses to keep their own 3 or the extra hand (before seeing the extra hand). The rejected 3 cards are turned face up and placed in the centre as the table pool. Dealing pattern: clockwise.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Have the highest-scoring three-card hand at the end of a hand (same-suit total, max 31, or three of a kind). Avoid losing chips; be the last player with chips to win the game.',
          gameplay: "1. Setup: Each player receives chips (e.g. 3 each). Deal 3 cards each plus dealer's extra hand; dealer's rejected 3 form the table pool.\n2. Play: Player to dealer's left acts first; turn passes clockwise. On your turn you may: (a) exchange one card with one table card, (b) exchange all three hand cards for the three table cards, or (c) pass. You may not exchange exactly two cards.\n3. Special combinations: Feuer (three aces = 32) or Schnauz (31 in one suit) must be exposed immediately and the hand ends.\n4. If all pass in succession, replace the three table cards with three from the talon and continue.\n5. A player may close at end of turn; then each other player gets one more turn and the hand ends.\n6. Scoring: Expose hands. Score = sum of one suit (or three of a kind: 30.5, except three aces = 32). Worst hand loses one chip. Feuer: all except holder lose a chip. Last chip lost = swimming; one more loss and you drop out. Last survivor wins.",
          keyRules: [
            'Exchange one card, all three, or pass; never exchange exactly two',
            'Feuer (three aces) and Schnauz (31 in one suit) end the hand immediately',
            'Lowest hand loses one chip; Feuer makes all others lose one chip',
            'Player who loses last chip is swimming; next loss eliminates them',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Improve your hand by swapping with the table; aim for 31 in one suit or three of a kind. Do not show reaction when someone takes a card you needed.',
          intermediate: 'Assume each player gets about three turns before someone closes. Form a plan and a backup (e.g. aim for three nines; if a nine is taken, switch to improving suit total). Watch which cards opponents take and discard to infer their targets.',
          advanced: 'Misdirect by staring at an unwanted card. If you must leave a high card, choose one that helps an opponent least. When swapping all three, opponents know your point total for the rest of the hand.',
          tips: [
            'Do not stare at the card you need; opponents will notice',
            'Games rarely last more than three rounds before someone closes',
            "Deduce opponents' strategies from their exchanges",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
